      "description": "DPF Monitor for VAG allows you to see several important data points relating to the Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) installed in a diesel vehicle built by VAG (Volkswagen, Audi, Skoda, and SEAT). By making this data visible it is possible to see the health of your DPF, as well as when an Active Regeneration is in progress.\n\nGETTING STARTED:\n\nStep 1: Connect your supported Bluetooth/WiFi OBD2 device\nStep 2: Open the application and select your device\nStep 3: Select a suitable engine group in the Settings menu\n\n\nSUPPORTED DEVICES:\n\nTo use the application, you require an OBD2 device with an ELM327 chip capable of communicating via the VAG UDS protocol. This device must support Bluetooth Low Energy (4.0+), or WiFi.\n\nVisit https://www.dpfmonitor.com/device-requirements for more details and recommended devices for purchase.\n\nNeed help finding a suitable dongle? Having connectivity issues? Please reach out to the developer for assistance!\n\n\nSUPPORTED ENGINES:\n\nThe following engine codes should be supported, although this is dependent on the software version installed to the ECU.\n\nCAAC, CAGA, CAHA, CAPA, CAYA, CAYB, CAYC, CCWA, CDSB, CFCA, CFFB, CFGB, CFGC, CFHA, CFHC, CFHD, CFJB, CFWA, CGLB, CGLC, CHNC, CJCA, CJCB, CJCD, CLAB, CLHA, CNHA, CNHC, CRBC, CRKB, CRLB, CRMB, CRUA, CSHA, CTBA, CUAA, CUDC, CUNA, CUPA, CUSA, CUSB, CUTA, CUUB, CUWA, CVUA, CVUB, CVUC, CXEB, CXEC, CXFA, CXHA, CXXA, CXXB, CZZA, DAUA, DAVA, DBGC, DBGC, DCPC, DCXA, DCYA, DDXC, DDXE, DDWA, DDYA, DETA, DEUA, DEUC, DEWA, DEZE, DFBA, DFCA, DFFA, DFGA, DFHA, DFLA, DFSB, DFSD, DFSF, DGDB, DSSA, DGTC, DGTD, DGTE, DHXA, DJGA, DLUB, DMZA, DMZB, DNAA, DSTB, DTRD, DTPB, DTSB, DTTC, DTUA, DXBA, DXNB, DXRB, DXRC, and many others.\n\nIs your engine code not showing as supported? Get in touch with the developer to join the Beta Programme and help out in getting it supported!\n\n\nGOT A QUESTION / SOMETHING NOT WORKING?\n\nContact the developer for assistance - I'm happy to help with any queries!",
